      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/6089a563f55824007016bdad/3adaae40-d8d6-4186-b166-96d6aa47d90f/16",
       "24x24": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/6089a563f55824007016bdad/3adaae40-d8d6-4186-b166-96d6aa47d90f/24",
       "32x32": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/6089a563f55824007016bdad/3adaae40-d8d6-4186-b166-96d6aa47d90f/32",
       "48x48": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/6089a563f55824007016bdad/3adaae40-d8d6-4186-b166-96d6aa47d90f/48"
      },
      "displayName": "André Schenk",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a563f55824007016bdad",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "We have a similar problem when we install Fedora into JBoss instead of Tomcat what we normally do with our eSciDoc installer. Then Fedora isn't deployed as long as the application server isn't running. But to do a Fedora rebuild it is necessary to stop Fedora before.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "I'd wish to have all dependent jar files available for the rebuild script even if no Tomcat evironment exists.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
